cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the derived tables, please cite this archived release."
title: "Reference-set dependence in reported co-annotation of lysine acylations: code and data"
abstract: "Analysis code and derived data supporting the manuscript of the same name. Using a published map of 88 lysine pyruvylation sites across 63 proteins, the archive supports comparisons of four reference designs, protein-stratified analyses across nine catalogue acylations, structural and annotation-evidence analyses, and an audit of reporting practice in 33 primary studies and nine reviews. Recalculation from archived derived tables is distinguished from re-extraction using upstream UniProt records and structural models."
